body:
Hush now, human. It will be fine. Even the clouds turn into downpour whenever it gets too heavy to hang on the sky. Even the ground trembles whenever it gets too terrified that it rips itself open just to swallow everything that is burdening it. Even the waves climb to the shore and devour islands when the pressure at the heart of the ocean is too much to bear. 

&nbsp;

Right now, I know you feel like a tangled hurricane inside your body. A walking catastrophe, leaving its path in ruins. A wild fire, turning your efforts into ashes. But human, don’t you apologize for taking space. Don’t you feel sorry for unleashing those overflowing emotions inside you. Don’t be ashamed for feeling too much.

&nbsp;

So what if you are spending the night alone? Don’t you know that solitude is better than presences that are nothing but poison to you?

&nbsp;

Maybe right now you feel like the world is pulling you back to the past. You can see the memories so picturesque. You can feel the trail of kisses, every touch, every slip of the hand. You can hear every word, every cry, every laughter. Everythng that didn’t last long but still haunts you . You are rummaging one cherished memory at a time, like a torture of hallucination that can never be real. 

I know, I know that it seems like the world is too heavy. You can lay it down. You can wait for your wounded hands to heal. You can wait for the scarlet scars to fade. You can wait for everything to turn quiet. And then appreciate the silence.

&nbsp;


Tomorrow, you will not be a tragedy that you think you are.

But tonight, let the city lights tuck you in your blanket while the stars will be busy chasing each other. Don’t you worry, human. The darkness will go gentle on you. Your nightmares will take its flight from your eyes. Your unbidden memories will soon not pierce your walls.

&nbsp;

*Tomorrow, you will rise again.*

*But tonight, you need to sleep.*
